{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:06196847fe549f64","name":"Forgotten Minefield","source":{"id":"source:reference-06196847fe549f64","title":"Forgotten Minefield","revision":21329,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:35:54Z","sha256":"a61967c8e1d2b4dbe405ba17d0d01a0c4ba03de105b02b9e7ed6f39f0e984f1b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21329","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Forgotten%20Minefield&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-06196847fe549f64","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Unseen explosive devices beneath the surface are triggered by creatures moving across the mines' trigger zones."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As a result of the ongoing conflict between the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Altiri"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Altiri","referenceId":"reference:261166585839a3f8"}," and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Anarrians"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Anarrians"},", there are many locations across the world that have been seeded with explosives as a deterrent against invasion. However, many times these minefields are left unmarked and are forgotten until some unaware citizen stumbles across a hidden mine. The following hazard can be used to add some spice to a combat encounter on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Altiria/Anarris"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Altiria/Anarris","referenceId":"reference:b486f69974791237"},", giving the heroes reason to be extra cautious during their movement across the battlefield.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Forgotten Minefield Statistics (CL 13)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Artificial"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Artificial"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Contact"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Contact"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Energy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Energy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fire","referenceId":"reference:c141faa80e43a119"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A being enters a square containing or adjacent to a Forgotten Mine; targeting the triggering being and any being in a square adjacent to the mine.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +15 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 6d6 (thrown 6 squares in random direction; Half Damage on Miss (thrown 3 squares in random direction))\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," On Trigger; once per mine\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," (DC 26):"]}," The character makes this check as a part of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},"; if the check succeeds, the character can enter squares adjacent to a Mine during that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"}," without triggering the Hazard."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," Each mine in the Forgotten Minefield should take up 1 square. There should be at least 1 mine per hero placed in the encounter area, plus additional mines for particularly large battlefields.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
